  "body": [
    "Fairtrade strives to support small-scale farmers and workers around the world. We work with more than 1,900 Producer Organisations, representing over two million smallholders and workers.",
    "Farming is the most important source of income and occupation for low-income households in rural areas. In fact, the livelihood of 40 percent of the global population depends on farming.",
    "Smallholders are small-scale farmers who manage areas varying from less than one hectare to 10 hectares which is managed at family level. It is used in part for production and to cover family needs.",
    "This also means that they compete in a global market to sell their produce. Where the benefits of trade are unevenly distributed. At the start of global supply chains, smallholders in regions like Africa, Latin America, Asia or the Middle East are facing challenging conditions, less bargaining power and precarious livelihoods. They are also hit hardest by the consequences of climate change.",
    "1/3 of the world’s food is produced by smallholder farmers.",
    "Despite their vital contribution, an unfair global market keeps many smallholder farmers in poverty, vulnerable to child labour, while their crops are under acute threat of climate change.",
    "Strong cooperatives Strong cooperatives In Fairtrade smallholder farmers are united in democratic producer organisations (cooperatives) which gives them stronger bargaining position, economic strengthening, knowledge exchange and support",
    "Fair Pricing Fair Pricing Fairtrade’s minimum price supports producers receiving a fair prices for their products and acts as a safety net when market prices drop. We also encourage long term contracts, which in turn support smallholder’s ability to plan ahead and invest in more sustainable practices.",
    "Decision making Decision making Producers are part of Fairtrade’s general assembly and hold 50% of the votes. They also have autonomy on how the Fairtrade Premium is used and invested in their community.",
    "Market Access Market Access Fairtrade connects producers to global markets, expanding sales opportunities and increasing incomes.",
    "Climate resilience Climate resilience Our standards and programmes foster agroecological farming practices. We also offer training for producers and strongly advocate at a governmental level for climate finance towards them.",
    "Fair working conditions Fair working conditions We advocate for worker’s rights, support child protection, and integrate health and safety within our standards.",
    "“In times of crisis, it becomes evident that Fairtrade enhances farmers’ economic resilience and supports them in continuing their profession in challenging times,” said Tatjana Mauthofer, researcher at Mainlevel Consulting and co-author of the study \"Assessing the Impact of Fairtrade on Poverty Reduction and Economic Resilience through Rural Development\".",
    "Fairtrade’s Impact on farmers and workers",
    "2022 Annual Report",
    "Executive summary: Sustainable agriculture under Fairtrade terms",
    "News: New Study Finds Fairtrade Enhances Farmer Resilience and Sustainability Amid Global Crises",
    "FAO: Smallholders and Family Farmers"
  ],
